0..65 Comment "// Equality derived from a data type\'s constructors: a definition"
66..137 Comment "// written `Eq.generic(T)` is structural equality over `T`, the checker"
138..209 Comment "// judging it as any declaration. Integers and strings compare by their"
210..289 Comment "// primitives, a sum by its side, a field of `T` itself recursively and a field"
290..356 Comment "// of another such type by that type\'s equality, written in place."
357..359 Comment "//"
360..437 Comment "// `Eq.generic.refl(T)` and `Eq.generic.sym(T)` prove that equality\'s laws by"
438..515 Comment "// congruence over `T`\'s constructors, resting on the laws the host admits of"
516..592 Comment "// integer and string equality, so a model of `Eq` whose members are derived"
593..670 Comment "// puts `T` under `==`. A field of a sum, as `Mark`\'s flag, or of `T` itself,"
671..749 Comment "// as `Peano`\'s, takes a proof the derivation does not write; the refusals are"
750..811 Comment "// beside `../../pathological/data/generic-eq-refused.gandr`."
812..814 Comment "//"
815..830 Comment "// - see: #2302"
